Validation of the beamstrahlung sampling and its shower interface
================================================================

dump.cc       showers an event file twice, with and without degrading the
              beams, and writes one line per event:
                  xbs1 xbs2 x1 x2 eCM sum(E_final) pT(mumu) sum(E_fwd_gamma)
makeplots.py  turns four such files into the validation figure

  # in the Pythia8 examples directory, built like the main itself
  ./dump events.lhe 20000 0 120.0 | grep '^[0-9]' > fcc_plain.dat
  ./dump events.lhe 20000 1 120.0 | grep '^[0-9]' > fcc_degr.dat
  #   ... and the same for an ILC sample into ilc_plain/ilc_degr.dat
  python3 makeplots.py

What each panel establishes:

  A  the sampled x_BS reproduces the CIRCE spectrum the grid was built
     from, over four decades
  B  Pythia's x equals x_LHE/x_BS to 7e-8, the precision of the 11-digit
     LHE momenta: the shower backward-evolves the ISR part only
  C  eCM matches sqrt(x_BS1 x_BS2 s) to 1e-11, and the final-state energy
     sums to (x_BS1+x_BS2)E rather than 2E
  D  ILC 500: the forward-photon energy the shower produces drops by
     8.4 GeV on average, against 9.3 GeV of beamstrahlung energy that left
     with the beam, and the fraction of events with no forward ISR photon
     at all goes from 26% to 43%
  E  FCC-ee 240: the two curves coincide, as they must when only 0.03 GeV
     is removed
  F  the beamstrahlung spectra behind D and E

Note that pT of the hard system is a poor observable here: it is dominated
by genuine hard ISR (radiative return to the Z) and the beamstrahlung shift
does not stand out above that tail.
